.TH KERO 1 "2026-09-01" "kero 0.1.0-alpha.1" "KERO User Manual"
.SH NAME
kero \- project-attached knowledge environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kero
.RI [ --help ]
.RI [ --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kero
is the command-line adapter for KERO, a persistent knowledge environment
attached to a project. KERO is being rebuilt around mounted heterogeneous
sources, provenance-preserving semantic knowledge, deterministic compilation,
queries, and bounded context projection.
.PP
The current pre-alpha binary exposes help and version information while typed
project, mount, source, semantic, compiler, status, query, and projection APIs
are implemented in planned phases. It does not yet expose stable product
commands or a stable storage format.
.SH PROJECT MODEL
A future KERO-aware tool discovers the nearest
.B .kero/
project boundary by walking upward from an explicit starting path. Reviewable
project configuration declares knowledge mounts. KERO owns compiled state,
indexes, and caches; users do not manually maintain an internal database tree.
.SH ARCHITECTURE
Human-readable sources are imported into a source-preserving model and semantic
IR. Canonicalization and canonical encoding are separate deterministic layers.
Indexes, summaries, embeddings, caches, and context projections are derived.
.PP
Source identity and provenance remain distinct. Conflicting claims coexist;
mount display order does not select a winner.
.SH INSTALLATION
Install from a source checkout with:
.PP
.EX
cargo install --path /path/to/kero-source/code/crates/kero-cli --locked
.EE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Print current command help.
.TP
.B --version
Print the package version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates successful argument processing. A nonzero status indicates an
invalid invocation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cargo (1),
.BR git (1)
